00:18:18.887 --> 00:18:20.857
"to take as an eighth
grader who wants to take

00:18:20.857 --> 00:18:23.197
"more advanced classes,
that will push him?"

00:18:24.568 --> 00:18:28.800
- Yeah, Angel, I would say you know

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:30.620
there was a previous question around

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:32.450
how much an eighth grader
could study, et cetera.

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:35.849
I mean I would, math is foundational

00:18:35.849 --> 00:18:38.010
for a lot of things.

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:41.300
So I would keep going on Khan
Academy as far as you can go.

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:43.340
If you're comfortable with
seventh, eighth grade,

00:18:43.340 --> 00:18:46.118
go on to algebra, go on to
algebra two, go on to geometry.

00:18:46.118 --> 00:18:48.640
That's going to give
you a good foundation.

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:50.480
I think you're really
looking to push yourself.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:51.710
You can start going into a lot of

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:54.500
the high school sciences
biology and chemistry.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:56.400
