for a group by different age groups.

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:00.190
So these are a list from the staff

00:23:00.190 --> 00:23:02.430
and recommendations from the staff.

00:23:02.430 --> 00:23:04.540
- And these are available,
correct me if I'm wrong,

00:23:04.540 --> 00:23:08.530
from our schedules and
we have the keep learning

00:23:08.530 --> 00:23:09.880
about Khan Academy at Oregon.

00:23:09.880 --> 00:23:11.590
People go there, you
dig around a little bit,

00:23:11.590 --> 00:23:13.730
you should find all of
these types of resources

00:23:13.730 --> 00:23:14.993
that we're talking about.

00:23:16.663 --> 00:23:20.840
So let's see, there's other sub receive.

00:23:20.840 --> 00:23:23.920
We have a from YouTube
Sattvic Agarwal says,

00:23:23.920 --> 00:23:26.387
"Hey, tell how did you
learn so many subjects

00:23:26.387 --> 00:23:27.357
"at such great depth?

00:23:27.357 --> 00:23:29.860
"What is your secret
to studying anything?"

00:23:29.860 --> 00:23:32.630
So the secret is to enjoy it.

00:23:32.630 --> 00:23:35.860
And when you enjoy it and
you're viewing yourself,

00:23:35.860 --> 00:23:36.847
you're not viewing yourself as like,

00:23:36.847 --> 00:23:39.387
"Oh, I got to memorize this
thing for tomorrow's test.

00:23:39.387 --> 00:23:40.280
"So that I don't feel."

00:23:40.280 --> 00:23:42.480
If you do it that way, it's not
gonna nothing is pleasurable

00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:43.660
if you do it that way.

00:23:43.660 --> 00:23:46.152
But if you say, wow,
there is this knowledge

00:23:46.152 --> 00:23:49.160
that for the last thousands of years

00:23:49.160 --> 00:23:50.840
humanity has been collecting

00:23:50.840 --> 00:23:52.135
and I have access to it

00:23:52.135 --> 00:23:55.301
and I get to ponder the
connections between the knowledge.

00:23:55.301 --> 00:23:58.382
I think for example, sometimes
things like textbooks,

00:23:58.382 --> 00:24:00.105
they have, they give you the knowledge

00:24:00.105 --> 00:24:02.290
but they don't connect the dots

00:24:02.290 --> 00:24:03.380
with things you already know.

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:05.006
And so I think it's actually
a fun exercise to ponder.

00:24:05.006 --> 00:24:08.128
I'm actually, that's the
favorite parts of my job now is

00:24:08.128 --> 00:24:11.681
if I'm trying to teach organic
chemistry for me to say,

00:24:11.681 --> 00:24:14.621
"So how does this mechanism connect to

00:24:14.621 --> 00:24:16.397
"what we learned before?

00:24:16.397 --> 00:24:17.847
"How are there some general themes here

00:24:17.847 --> 00:24:19.950
"that the book is saying?"

00:24:19.950 --> 00:24:22.820
and what you find is when you
ponder it for a little bit

00:24:22.820 --> 00:24:24.610
and just ask people questions,

00:24:24.610 --> 00:24:25.990
some of those connections for them

00:24:25.990 --> 00:24:27.582
and you get to be a
little bit of a detective.

00:24:27.582 --> 00:24:31.900
I view almost everything
on Khan Academy and beyond

00:24:31.900 --> 00:24:34.142
as we're trying to understand this mystery

00:24:34.142 --> 00:24:38.630
that we find ourselves
in called called life

00:24:38.630 --> 00:24:40.889
and the universe, and as human beings,

00:24:40.889 --> 00:24:43.580
I don't think there's
anything more fulfilling

00:24:43.580 --> 00:24:45.260
than trying to make sense of that.

00:24:45.260 --> 00:24:47.180
And yes, sometimes some of the ways

00:24:47.180 --> 00:24:49.616
that we get exposed to
some of the mysteries,

00:24:49.616 --> 00:24:51.820
whether it's in textbooks or other ways,

00:24:51.820 --> 00:24:53.090
it might be a little bit cryptic,

00:24:53.090 --> 00:24:54.030
but that's fun too.

00:24:54.030 --> 00:24:55.922
You know, when you watch
a protagonist in a movie

00:24:55.922 --> 00:24:57.713
and they come up with some hieroglyphics,

00:24:57.713 --> 00:24:59.463
they don't just say, "Oh,
this is hard to read.

00:24:59.463 --> 00:25:01.346
"I'm going to give up and
go do something else."

00:25:01.346 --> 00:25:03.680
And I'm like, this is exciting.

00:25:03.680 --> 00:25:04.850
This is an adventure.

00:25:04.850 --> 00:25:06.404
When Harry Potter discovers
a spell book or whatever,

00:25:06.404 --> 00:25:08.051
it's not like they just give up.

00:25:08.051 --> 00:25:09.479
They're like, "How do we read this thing?

00:25:09.479 --> 00:25:11.410
"How does this connect to other things?"

00:25:11.410 --> 00:25:13.460
So I kind of view learning that way.

00:25:13.460 --> 00:25:15.247
And I have found a lot of folks say,

00:25:15.247 --> 00:25:18.046
"Oh, I'm a math person, or
I'm a humanities person."

00:25:18.046 --> 00:25:22.430
I actually think if you
stereotype yourself in that way,

00:25:22.430 --> 00:25:23.980
you're doing yourself an injustice.

00:25:23.980 --> 00:25:25.241
And I've been guilty of it myself.

00:25:25.241 --> 00:25:27.290
Early on in my life,

00:25:27.290 --> 00:25:29.352
I didn't view myself as someone
who really enjoyed writing,

00:25:29.352 --> 00:25:31.090
but now I do.

00:25:31.090 --> 00:25:33.340
And the way that I kind
of made that transition

00:25:33.340 --> 00:25:35.150
is to realize that,

00:25:35.150 --> 00:25:37.350
when I was writing just to
try to impress someone else

00:25:37.350 --> 00:25:38.570
just to try to get a grade,

00:25:38.570 --> 00:25:39.860
I wasn't enjoying it that much.

00:25:39.860 --> 00:25:41.800
But when I realized that writing

00:25:41.800 --> 00:25:44.417
is really just a way
to get my point across,

00:25:44.417 --> 00:25:47.998
to communicate something or
to express my imagination,

00:25:47.998 --> 00:25:50.460
then all of a sudden it
became super exciting

00:25:50.460 --> 00:25:53.420
and it's not one of my
favorite activities to write

00:25:53.420 --> 00:25:55.540
or to communicate in other ways.

00:25:55.540 --> 00:25:58.480
So I think it's all about
a mindset to realize

00:25:58.480 --> 00:26:00.700
that very few people
are either math people

00:26:00.700 --> 00:26:02.790
or writing people or humanities people.

00:26:02.790 --> 00:26:05.550
Once you're used to learning any subject,

00:26:05.550 --> 00:26:07.210
you can apply that, that same muscle

00:26:07.210 --> 00:26:09.760
to almost everything else
and see the beauty in it.

