from a YouTube Nickel Govendor,

00:26:49.217 --> 00:26:51.526
"Who's your favorite superhero?"

00:26:51.526 --> 00:26:53.750
So not having thought about it

00:26:53.750 --> 00:26:55.350
more than the last five seconds.

00:26:55.350 --> 00:27:00.350
I have had an affinity to,
I think Batman's interesting

00:27:00.470 --> 00:27:02.716
because he kind of has a
growth mindset about things

00:27:02.716 --> 00:27:06.883
like he is not born
with any innate ability

00:27:06.883 --> 00:27:09.670
but he leverages the
resources he does have.

00:27:09.670 --> 00:27:11.800
And I guess he, well, he
was born with resources

00:27:11.800 --> 00:27:13.720
according to the Batman legend.

00:27:13.720 --> 00:27:17.313
But he's focused on improving himself

00:27:17.313 --> 00:27:19.780
and becoming much stronger

00:27:19.780 --> 00:27:22.610
than whatever innate
abilities he might have.

00:27:22.610 --> 00:27:25.670
So I think there's something
very powerful about that,

00:27:25.670 --> 00:27:29.560
but I'm sure I'm forgetting
many other superheroes

00:27:29.560 --> 00:27:32.513
that are quite compelling.

00:27:33.973 --> 00:27:36.897
So, Anjani asking another question.

00:27:36.897 --> 00:27:39.047
"What's advice you would give to students

00:27:39.047 --> 00:27:41.656
"who are stressed about the situation?"

00:27:41.656 --> 00:27:45.653
The best thing to
realize is, first of all,

00:27:45.653 --> 00:27:47.510
you're not alone, that's
helped me sometimes

00:27:47.510 --> 00:27:48.640
when I started getting a little worried

00:27:48.640 --> 00:27:49.800
about certain family members

00:27:49.800 --> 00:27:52.440
who might be living by
themselves or they have a cough.

00:27:52.440 --> 00:27:55.010
All of a sudden I'm like,
Oh no do they have COVID?

00:27:55.010 --> 00:27:57.470
Is that we're all in this together.

00:27:57.470 --> 00:27:59.841
And all you can do in life generally

00:27:59.841 --> 00:28:02.179
to quote "Frozen 1" and "Frozen 2" is,

00:28:02.179 --> 00:28:07.179
if you can't control a
situation to kind of let it go,

00:28:07.800 --> 00:28:09.910
don't try to think too much about it.

00:28:09.910 --> 00:28:11.570
If it's out of your sphere of control

00:28:11.570 --> 00:28:14.210
and of the things that are
in your sphere of control,

00:28:14.210 --> 00:28:15.242
do the next right thing.

00:28:15.242 --> 00:28:17.915
And then the chips fall where they do.

00:28:17.915 --> 00:28:22.630
In Vedic philosophy, there's
this notion of action.

00:28:22.630 --> 00:28:26.020
There's a Rajasic action where
you're focused on the outcome

00:28:26.020 --> 00:28:29.030
and then there's Sattvic action, which is,

00:28:29.030 --> 00:28:30.970
in Sanskrit, it's truthful action

00:28:30.970 --> 00:28:32.220
which is you're doing it

00:28:32.220 --> 00:28:33.540
just because it's the right thing to do

00:28:33.540 --> 00:28:35.550
regardless of what the outcome is.

00:28:35.550 --> 00:28:37.580
And I think a lot of our stress in life,

00:28:37.580 --> 00:28:40.370
a lot of our anxiety in life,
a lot of our suffering in life

00:28:40.370 --> 00:28:42.350
happens because we get
attached to outcomes.

00:28:42.350 --> 00:28:43.860
We're like, "Oh, that
thing has to happen."

00:28:43.860 --> 00:28:45.650
And then, "Oh, what if it doesn't happen?"

00:28:45.650 --> 00:28:47.940
And then you start
procrastinating, you get stressed,

00:28:47.940 --> 00:28:49.220
you get anxious about it.

00:28:49.220 --> 00:28:52.810
But if you just say, look,
none of us have control

00:28:52.810 --> 00:28:55.260
over the universe, over this world,

00:28:55.260 --> 00:28:57.280
all we can do is just the next right thing

00:28:57.280 --> 00:28:58.820
and we do the next right thing

00:28:58.820 --> 00:29:01.364
and just accept wherever the chips fall

00:29:01.364 --> 00:29:04.659
is one way to keep moving forward

00:29:04.659 --> 00:29:08.100
and doing the right thing
without getting overwhelmed.

00:29:08.100 --> 00:29:09.210
The other thing I would recommend

00:29:09.210 --> 00:29:12.741
is things like meditation exercise.

00:29:12.741 --> 00:29:16.550
These are great ways to steal your mind,

00:29:16.550 --> 00:29:20.070
to get your mind out of
some of the thought patterns

00:29:20.070 --> 00:29:21.818
that a lot of folks
experiencing right now.

00:29:21.818 --> 00:29:25.340
I would recommend minimize
watching the news.

00:29:25.340 --> 00:29:27.080
You know, most of us know what's going on.

00:29:27.080 --> 00:29:29.890
It doesn't hurt to watch
for 20 minutes a day

00:29:29.890 --> 00:29:30.723
or something like that.

00:29:30.723 --> 00:29:32.580
Say, okay, that's what's going on there.

00:29:32.580 --> 00:29:33.980
That's what the government's doing.

00:29:33.980 --> 00:29:36.010
But I think if you watch too much of it,

00:29:36.010 --> 00:29:37.507
the news is almost designed to keep you

00:29:37.507 --> 00:29:41.950
in this state of anxiety and the state of

00:29:43.490 --> 00:29:46.640
that we this get your cortisol level up.

00:29:46.640 --> 00:29:47.990
That normally only happens in nature

00:29:47.990 --> 00:29:49.430
when a bear is chasing you,

00:29:49.430 --> 00:29:50.980
which doesn't happen too often

00:29:50.980 --> 00:29:52.600
if you were just wandering the forest.

00:29:52.600 --> 00:29:55.081
But it's good for ratings
cause it gets you engaged.

00:29:55.081 --> 00:29:57.380
But it could be bad
for your mental health.

00:29:57.380 --> 00:29:59.357
So I would say spend as much time outside

00:29:59.357 --> 00:30:01.159
exercising time with family,

00:30:01.159 --> 00:30:03.409
stay connected through video conferencing

00:30:03.409 --> 00:30:07.069
to friends and family,
meditate as much as you can

00:30:07.069 --> 00:30:10.190
and also remind yourself
don't get caught up with stuff

00:30:10.190 --> 00:30:12.271
that is out of your sphere of control

00:30:12.271 --> 00:30:14.320
just stay within your sphere of control

00:30:14.320 --> 00:30:16.017
and say, "What's the
next right thing I can do

00:30:16.017 --> 00:30:17.647
"and feel good about that?"

